The '''2026''' '''Kingston upon Thames London Borough Council election''' took place on 7 May 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-01 |title=Local elections in London will test support for Reform UK and Greens |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c99k0mzj7x8o |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> All 48 members of [[Kingston upon Thames London Borough Council]] were elected. The elections took place alongside [[2026 London local elections|local elections in the other London boroughs]] and [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|elections to local authorities across the United Kingdom]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Number of councils that have requested delay to local elections revealed - is yours one of them? |url=https://news.sky.com/story/local-elections-2026-over-a-third-of-councils-offered-a-delay-have-requested-one-is-yours-on-the-list-13494762 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Sky News |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In 2022 the [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] retained control of Kingston upon Thames council.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Kingston-upon-Thames result - Local Elections 2022 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2022/england/councils/E09000021 |access-date=2026-01-19 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> The Conservatives formed the opposition with three seats.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-05-07 |title=Liberal Democrats hold Kingston with 41 seats won in local election |url=https://www.surreycomet.co.uk/news/20122137.kingston-local-election-results-2022-liberal-democrats-hold/ |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Surrey Comet |language=en}}</ref>

